+# AGENTS.md (Codex)
+
+Read `CLAUDE.md` first. Its project rules, permissions, protected-file boundaries and containment
+procedures apply to Codex just as they apply to Claude Code.
+
+## Owner-authorized contained execution (2026-10-20)
+
+The owner authorizes Codex to build, test, research and exercise the client and servers end to end
+using the same installed hook-enforced containment workflow as Claude Code. There is no additional
+Codex-only prohibition on running the game, codecs, tests or servers, and no extra confirmation is
+needed merely because the agent is Codex.
+
+- Game code, codec workers and their tests run only through the installed root-owned
+  `/usr/local/libexec/d1-agent/d1-nonet`, as one plain launcher command, following `CLAUDE.md`.
+- Other programs that listen or connect use `/usr/local/libexec/d1-agent/d1-localonly` as required
+  by `CLAUDE.md`. Ordinary source inspection and builds use the normal agent sandbox.
+- When Codex's outer sandbox cannot apply the installed launcher policy, use the supported
+  approval-managed execution route for that launcher-wrapped command. The game/test/server
+  must remain inside its installed containment; never run it bare or request
+  `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox`.
+- A refusal from any gate, launcher or hook is a finding to report, never an obstacle to work
+  around. An unavailable approval review does not authorize another execution route.
+- Protected files remain owner-controlled under `CLAUDE.md`. This requested instructions update
+  does not authorize changing installed hooks, launchers, profiles, C gates or their build glue.
+- Access to real networks or another machine still requires the owner's explicit authorization
+  in the session. Contained local execution is not permission to reach the internet.
+
+These instructions record the owner's authorization; they do not grant privileges beyond the
+current tool permissions, approval policy or installed containment controls.
